(1)       0 :                    ;;; -*- mode: asm; mode: flyspell-prog; -*-
(1)       0 :                    ;;; The CP/M-8000 BIOS for the Z8001: the console on the i8251 and four
(1)       0 :                    ;;; drives on the debugger's sector disk, both polled, byte I/O at 16-bit
(1)       0 :                    ;;; port addresses. cpm8000bios.asm links it with DRI's 1.1 kernel as DRI
(1)       0 :                    ;;; shipped it for the Olivetti M20, pcpm8000bios.asm with the 1.2 kernel
(1)       0 :                    ;;; built from P-CP/M-Z8K's sources with the M20's glue; either runs
(1)       0 :                    ;;; nonsegmented in system mode in segment 0 and calls the BIOS with SC
(1)       0 :                    ;;; #3: R3 the function, RR4 and RR6 the parameters, the result back in
(1)       0 :                    ;;; RR6 (R7 for a word). SC #2 is the BDOS, SC #1 memory management and
(1)       0 :                    ;;; the context switch that starts a program. Traps enter segmented, as
(1)       0 :                    ;;; the Z8001 takes them; the dispatcher saves the M20's frame and calls
(1)       0 :                    ;;; each handler segmented, as the kernel's own trap glue expects. `cpu
(1)       0 :                    ;;; z8001` marks code that runs segmented, `cpu z8002` code that runs
(1)       0 :                    ;;; nonsegmented.
(1)       0 :
